===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|ga|Lú|alt=Lugh}}, from {{der|en|sga|Lug}}, from {{der|en|pgl|ᚂᚒᚌ}}, from {{der|en|cel-pro|*Lugus}}.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{lb|en|Irish mythology}} A pre-Christian Irish deity represented in [[mythological]] texts as a hero and [[High King]] of the distant past: the son of [[Cian]] and [[Ethniu]].

